6d8a6b80-b68c-49ef-b46a-dd4486e21548	01_glass_transition_thermal_properties	textbook	en	The parameter T0 is often interpreted as the ideal glass transition temperature, below which the viscosity would theoretically become infinite. For soda-lime-silica glass, typical VFT parameters are: A = -2.485, B = 4545, T0 = 268 (temperatures in Celsius). These parameters allow calculation of viscosity at any temperature within the forming range. 2.1 Viscosity Reference Points in Glass Manufacturing Reference Point Viscosity (Pa.s) Temperature (C) Significance Melting point 10^1 - 10^2 1400-1600 Glass melting in furnace Working point 10^3 1000-1200 Forming operations Softening point 10^6.6 700-900 Sagging under own weight Dilatometric Tg 10^10 - 10^11 500-600 Thermal expansion change Annealing point 10^12 450-550 Stress relief temperature Strain point 10^13.5 400-500 Lower limit of annealing Glass Expert AI -- Sample Document | Page 3 Glass Transition Temperature and Thermal Properties Chapter 3: Thermal Expansion of Glass The coefficient of thermal expansion (CTE) is a measure of how much a material expands or contracts per unit length per degree of temperature change.	{"file_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\Documents\\\\Projects\\\\glass-expert-ai-phase1\\\\glass-expert-ai\\\\data\\\\sample_docs\\\\01_glass_transition_thermal_properties.pdf", "page_count": 4, "chunk_index": 5, "ingested_at": "2026-03-04T13:49:03.627037", "total_chunks": 8}	[-0.0041965456,0.031454235,0.03653194,0.037171137,-0.058172937,-0.015004415,-0.013388194,0.008022915,-0.02852673,0.06622859,-0.0015902267,0.021314928,0.014825093,-0.05890652,-0.017833356,0.03905282,-0.008487448,0.008653631,-0.051071692,0.04245102,-0.004307382,0.033161674,-0.057085074,-0.042598814,-0.029797543,0.008423624,0.0024445713,-0.03904715,0.10989721,0.027802907,0.003206947,-0.024015807,0.0075929533,-0.07604176,2.4993755e-05,0.008060111,0.02761486,-0.056720827,-0.02288868,-0.05385546,0.05041562,-0.00029873164,0.04168084,0.00041667346,-0.0377279