1b826eef-6345-4267-bdb0-97ab26c99b24	03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop	sop	en	Common fining agents include: - Sodium sulfate (Na2SO4): Releases SO2/SO3 at high temperature, creating large bubbles that rise quickly and carry smaller bubbles with them. - Arsenic trioxide (As2O3): Releases O2 during cooling, absorbing residual bubbles. - Antimony trioxide (Sb2O3): Similar mechanism to arsenic, used as a safer alternative. - Cerium oxide (CeO2): Releases O2 at fining temperatures. - Tin oxide (SnO2): Used in lead-free crystal glass. 2.1 Bubble Defect Troubleshooting Guide Bubble Type Gas Content Location Root Cause Corrective Action Seeds SO2/O2 Throughout Insufficient fining Increase fining agent, raise temp Blisters Surface Reboil from sulfate Reduce sulfate, check redox CO2 seeds Bottom Incomplete melting Increase melt temp/time O2 bubbles Random Reboil on reheating Adjust forming temperature Large bubbles Mixed Refractory reaction Inspect refractory Glass Expert AI -- Sample Document | Page 2 Glass Manufacturing Defects -- Identification & Troubleshooting	{"file_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\Documents\\\\Projects\\\\glass-expert-ai-phase1\\\\glass-expert-ai\\\\data\\\\sample_docs\\\\03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop.pdf", "page_count": 4, "chunk_index": 4, "ingested_at": "2026-03-04T13:49:48.801649", "total_chunks": 10}	[-0.007688285,0.033077102,0.00055481767,0.033673506,-0.077865444,-0.037450235,-0.021695148,-0.019992732,0.017284147,0.040301435,-0.011046567,-0.01053498,0.020779165,-0.036379803,-0.010280008,-0.036747713,0.008192693,0.018729726,-0.030455086,-0.028428275,0.021556143,0.00021208334,-0.032096293,-0.014373879,-0.026431097,-0.01177278,-0.046577077,-0.022627315,0.05799905,0.03665834,-0.023207916,-0.0058878497,0.04982113,-0.03646206,0.0005934821,-0.01680499,0.026177822,-0.016826838,-0.025640666,-0.039189126,0.024954276,0.0023349798,0.07703023,-0.021232031,-0.034456447,-0.027634818,-0.021479417,-0.009524686,-0.023109797,-0.02707871,-0.002381259,0.013914813,0.0