17b4f263-26af-4733-95a3-e0b8269ef906	03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop	sop	en	Cristobalite (SiO2) can also form at higher temperatures in silica-rich compositions. PREVENTION METHODS: 1. Composition control: Maintain composition within the stable glass-forming region. Avoid compositions near eutectic points in the phase diagram. 2. Nucleating agent control: Minimize the presence of nucleating agents such as TiO2, ZrO2, and P2O5 unless intentional (as in glass-ceramics). 3. Cooling rate control: Cool through the devitrification temperature range as quickly as possible to minimize residence time. 4. Surface cleanliness: Devitrification often initiates at the glass surface. Maintain clean forming tools and avoid contamination. 5. Redox control: Maintain appropriate redox conditions in the melt to prevent precipitation of crystalline phases. Glass Expert AI -- Sample Document | Page 3 Glass Manufacturing Defects -- Identification & Troubleshooting SOP Section 4: Cord, Striae, and Knots Cord and striae are inhomogeneities in the glass that appear as thread-like or layered regions with a slightly different refractive index from the surrounding glass. They are caused by local variations in chemical composition within the glass melt.	{"file_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\Documents\\\\Projects\\\\glass-expert-ai-phase1\\\\glass-expert-ai\\\\data\\\\sample_docs\\\\03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop.pdf", "page_count": 4, "chunk_index": 7, "ingested_at": "2026-03-04T13:49:48.939915", "total_chunks": 10}	[-0.023199674,0.035598703,0.02112873,0.0380299,-0.032373674,-0.030090176,-0.04446454,-0.022104079,0.010801801,0.06340525,0.0006468362,0.004668549,0.037462313,-0.033800226,-0.027408611,0.013853419,-0.004222193,0.014900826,-0.044188425,0.047022004,0.011618007,0.013132926,-0.036546495,-0.0329234,-0.059786845,0.026763843,-0.02429534,-0.016067732,0.08664115,0.00977893,-0.050411973,0.004130028,0.045483105,-0.02759335,-0.021877615,-0.01910669,0.034672827,0.013562926,0.016326234,-0.085865