6e962a67-4a6b-4411-af35-42f43ec41218	03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop	sop	en	They are caused by local variations in chemical composition within the glass melt. IDENTIFICATION: Cord appears as visible threads or layers when the glass is viewed in transmitted light against a dark background. Striae are finer, more subtle variations that may require schlieren photography or interferometry to detect. Both defects cause optical distortion and are unacceptable in precision optical glass. CAUSES: 1. Incomplete mixing of batch materials: Regions of different composition in the melt that have not been fully homogenized. 2. Refractory dissolution: Silica or alumina dissolved from furnace refractories creates high-viscosity regions that resist mixing. 3. Volatilization: Loss of volatile components (B2O3, PbO, alkali oxides) from the melt surface creates a surface layer with different composition. 4. Cullet inhomogeneity: Use of cullet with different composition from the batch.	{"file_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\Documents\\\\Projects\\\\glass-expert-ai-phase1\\\\glass-expert-ai\\\\data\\\\sample_docs\\\\03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop.pdf", "page_count": 4, "chunk_index": 8, "ingested_at": "2026-03-04T13:49:48.988736", "total_chunks": 10}	[-0.01711253,0.008623367,0.017187482,0.047988355,-0.053113606,0.0020833309,-0.028372148,-0.026379755,0.0056660995,0.073775396,0.02131817,-0.013800745,0.012770439,-0.033003397,-0.048920248,0.039789934,-0.020792505,-0.0132795945,-0.057360265,0.010109217,0.013171754,0.0078013246,-0.037233077,-0.026235033,-0.00674329,0.04906167,0.028035894,-0.004480426,0.04853682,0.028693166,-0.029172461,0.021513566,0.01829889,-0.058348026,0.0065816357,0.022384671,0.02263077,-0.010507545,-0.018981956,-0.09153769,0.046687644,0.018244704,0.021623563,-0.04590638,-0.02955334,-0.036934428,0.0077130594,-0.04195194,-0.018606534,0.0027136651,-0.0065589896,-0.02190351,0.047109786,-0.04853669,-0.023556247,0.033124402,-0.034713946,0.012798314,-0.026406454,-0.05668165,0.0