9fcafaa0-eed1-4b8e-a33e-f3c83ec73269	03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop	sop	en	Volatilization: Loss of volatile components (B2O3, PbO, alkali oxides) from the melt surface creates a surface layer with different composition. 4. Cullet inhomogeneity: Use of cullet with different composition from the batch. CORRECTIVE ACTIONS: - Improve batch mixing and homogeneity - Increase stirring in the refining zone - Reduce refractory corrosion by adjusting melt chemistry - Control volatilization by adjusting furnace atmosphere - Ensure cullet composition matches batch composition 4.1 Summary of Glass Defect Types and Severity Defect Type Visual Appearance Severity Primary Cause Stones Opaque solid inclusions Critical Undissolved batch/refractory Bubbles/Seeds Spherical voids High Incomplete fining Blisters Large surface bubbles High Reboil/sulfate Devitrification Crystalline haze/crust Critical Composition/cooling Cord Visible threads/layers Moderate-High Compositional inhomogeneity Striae Fine optical distortion Moderate Minor comp. variation Knots Dense glassy inclusions High Refractory dissolution Wires Metallic inclusions Critical Metal contamination Glass Expert AI -- Sample Document | Page 4	{"file_path": "C:\\\\Users\\\\Documents\\\\Projects\\\\glass-expert-ai-phase1\\\\glass-expert-ai\\\\data\\\\sample_docs\\\\03_glass_defects_troubleshooting_sop.pdf", "page_count": 4, "chunk_index": 9, "ingested_at": "2026-03-04T13:49:49.039362", "total_chunks": 10}	[-0.019958526,0.0031040823,-0.01249403,0.0322087,-0.032567628,-0.0059885173,-0.009622869,-0.013308583,0.011143905,0.02349934,0.01754417,0.0016516044,0.020378608,-0.027284909,-0.039264433,-0.0027025728,-0.02383036,0.00046002815,-0.061560415,-0.011975405,-0.006900732,0.0054333904,-0.0441216,-0.026597869,-0.01586606,0.04633037,-0.027284492,0.0029442587,0.09974451,0.0529094,-0.036505815,0.0029514497,0.00427572,-0.05033163,0.008970948,0.0043048877,0.015979446,0.00696325,-0.019773116,-0.050192665,0.062300276,0.02408073,0.010100